          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On the evening of March 21, 2009, in a clear sky without clouds, a witness had their photo taken. Upon reviewing the digital photo, the witness was intrigued by a white patch in the sky visible in the image. As there was no direct observation during the photo's capture, the primary hypothesis is that an insect or a small bird, close to the subject at the time of the flash, passed through the field of view. The insect would have been intensely illuminated by the flash. This case is classified as \"B\": probable passage of an insect within the camera's field of view.",
